                    <h3>What is a Recurring Investment?</h3>
                    <p>
                        A Recurring Investment is a way to save or invest a fixed amount at regular intervals, such as monthly. Instead of investing a large amount at one time, you can contribute smaller amounts regularly according to the selected plan.
                    </p>

                    <ul>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>Helps develop a regular and disciplined saving habit.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>Allows you to invest or save smaller amounts at regular intervals.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>Can help build savings gradually over a selected period.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>Can be planned according to different financial goals and requirements.</span></li>
                    </ul>

                    <p>
                        Recurring investments can be useful for goals such as children's education, future expenses, emergency savings, travel planning, retirement planning, or other financial requirements. Regular contributions can help create a structured approach to saving over time.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Before choosing a Recurring Investment, consider the contribution amount, frequency, investment period, expected returns, risk level, withdrawal conditions, charges, taxation, and other applicable terms. The features and returns may vary depending on the selected financial product.
                    </p>
